[Opening "Caro-Kann Defense: Exchange Variation, Rubinstein Variation"]
[StudyName "🏰 Caro-Kann Defense🔥"]
[ChapterName "Exchange Variation"]
[ChapterURL "https://lichess.org/study/jtlLwUvh/ZHFnZdk9"]
[Annotator "https://lichess.org/@/LeninPerez"]
[UTCDate "2021.02.03"]
[UTCTime "17:02:14"]
[ChapterMode "gamebook"]

1. e4 { Make the first moves :) } 1... c6 2. d4 d5 3. exd5 { This is the Exchange Variation.
The white player prefers to be in an open position.
Capture the pawn } { [%cal Be4d5] } 3... cxd5 4. Bd3 { Develop your knight } { [%csl Gb8] } 4... Nc6 5. c3 { The white player with c3 defends the pawn on d5.
Develop your other knight } { [%cal Gc3d4] } 5... Nf6 6. Bf4 { It's time to develop your bishop } { [%csl Gc8] } 6... Bg4 { Very well! This is one of the ways to play for the white player, as there is a quick 4.f4 in this variation. } *


